more interested in W5 if it literally ditched the racist, sexist, and self-pitying werewolves and became a game about the Mokole rising and taking the lead against the Wyrm - movie level demolition of landmarks and tourist attractions and all. Release it as an alternative universe supplement, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou prejudices and habits tend to be a bit skewed away from those and toward celebrating shooting themselves in the foot because of the glorious traditional ballads of the Wars of Rage and other bull-headed rampages. Self-pity is, hence, sparse, and likely a sign of falling to Harano.<br /> <br /> But as much as the lore built up around the end of Revised suggests that the Mokole would tend to awaken and take charge around this sort of time in the cycle of boom and bust of civilizations, it's unlikely that we'd get that even an alternate campaign setting. Changing Ways got declared non-canonical because the first round of folks from Paradox who were in charge of WW stuff didn't want its past for whatever reason, and it's seemed that from the very beginning, those same people didn't like Revised-era material very much. Between that and a nebulous up-turning of the nose at anything that might be termed &quot;urban fantasy&quot;, the community would have to put this together independent of corporate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T19:30:06-08:00","id":1362992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot